# STIG RHEL-09-232260: no-ww-dirs-no-sticky
# STIG ID: V-257932 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `r9-rhel-09-232260-no-ww-dirs-no-sticky-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG RHEL-09-232260: RHEL 9 must be configured so that all system device files are correctly labeled `
    description `RHEL 9 must be configured so that all system device files are correctly labeled to prevent unauthorized modification.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `rhel9,stig,disa-stig,filesystem`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:RHEL-09-232260,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `CM-6`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:os-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for RHEL-09-232260.`

    component_id `comp-r9-os`

    impl_CM_6 `This control is validated by checking the required system configuration against the DISA STIG baseline for RHEL 9.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT fs_scan
        scan_type `world_writable_dirs_no_sticky`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE scan_clean
        found boolean = true
        match_count int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN filesystem_scan
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF scan_clean
            OBJECT_REF fs_scan
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
